" =============================================================================
" 04-previews.vifm -- quick view (w) and view mode
" =============================================================================
"
" All previewing funnels through scripts/preview, which dispatches on MIME type
" and degrades gracefully when an optional tool is missing. Keeping it in one
" script rather than spreading ~20 :fileviewer rules across this file means the
" dispatch logic is testable on its own:
"
"     ~/.config/vifm/scripts/preview <file> <width> <height>
"
" vifm adds scripts/ to $PATH, so the bare name resolves.
"
" %c:p -- absolute path of the current file
" %pw  -- width of the preview area
" %ph  -- height of the preview area
"
" Deliberately no %px/%py: a previewer containing both is treated by vifm as a
" *graphics* previewer. The image path uses chafa in symbol mode (plain text),
" which is what makes previews work inside tmux, so vifm should treat the
" output as ordinary text.
fileviewer */ preview %c:p %pw %ph
fileviewer *  preview %c:p %pw %ph

" Symbol-mode output is text, so no delay is needed before drawing and nothing
" lingers that would require a hard clear. Cap preview trees so that previewing
" a huge directory cannot stall the UI.
set previewoptions=graphicsdelay:0,maxtreedepth:3

" Man pages render better through the real pager pipeline than through `file`.
fileviewer {*.[1-8]},<text/troff> man ./%c | col -b
